\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,{e}^{-t},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}{{e}^{t}})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3}}}{{e}^{3t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132051" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a7e2dc04-d285-5815-98e3-c99d4176897c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484263 #edb/ref 1074 "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =4\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =4⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =8⟨1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =(4⟨2t,\\,1,\\,0⟩)\\times (8⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩) \\\\  & =32\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2t & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =32\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-32\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=32.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{{(4\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{64\\sqrt{{(4{t}^{2}+1)}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{(4{t}^{2}+1)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484304 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484304 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0d33b287-b538-55b3-b3c7-cf0142e26701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484304 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186354511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484328 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484328 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "723416d5-8258-5723-a84d-1b6f2871325d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484328 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484334 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484334 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e9f96eb-3033-5b55-bf1d-bd63b264150d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484334 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186368805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484347 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186484361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484347 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bdfbf0ab-5e71-5eab-a28e-ae335d919cc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484347 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186484251 #edb/ref 175921860454